<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RUT_WastelandFlora — COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1 wave 11, wasteland sheet.
    Two of wasteland.md §"Radiotrophs"'s named flora: the dosimeter-lawn (growth
    marks the hottest ground) and the vault-root sequestration tree (roots
    concentrate what the plants absorb into a mineable "vault ore"). Plain
    vanilla PlantBase/TreeBase, no `<pollution>` gate — same reasoning as
    RUT_PollutedFlora.xml's own header: Biotech's runtime "Polluted" tile state
    is an event-driven mechanic these biome themes don't mean by "poisoned
    ground," and gating on it would make these plants effectively never spawn
    wild.

    The dosimeter-lawn's actual growth-correlates-with-radiation-dose behaviour
    and the vault-root's actual ore-mining mechanic are BOTH the "dose/geiger
    layer" wasteland.md's own Owed section already names as engine-feasibility
    work — ships now as ordinary flora (RUT_VaultRoot yields WoodLog like every
    other wood-harvest tree in this mod's rosters), hooks later, same posture
    RUT_BloomCrop (this item, wave 10) used for its own deferred flood mechanic.
    Not filed as a second item — it's the same open scope wasteland.md already
    names.

    Working defNames only — wasteland.md's own "Owed: Names, owner's pick"
    line explicitly includes "the radiotroph flora" among five things still
    needing the owner's name; folded into WASTELAND_SHIPPING_NAMES_1.
  -->

  <!-- ============== Dosimeter lawn (ground cover) — RUT_Wasteland ============== -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="PlantBase">
    <defName>RUT_DosimeterLawn</defName>
    <label>dosimeter lawn</label>
    <description>A low mat of sickly, unnervingly vivid moss-lichen. It grows thickest over the hottest ground -- locals read its color and density as a rough gauge of what's buried beneath, and camp where it refuses to grow at all.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>85</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0.8</Flammability>
      <Nutrition>0.35</Nutrition>
    </statBases>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Plant/DosimeterLawn</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Random</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>1.1</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <hideAtSnowOrSandDepth>0.5</hideAtSnowOrSandDepth>
    <selectable>false</selectable>
    <plant>
      <growDays>3</growDays>
      <harvestWork>40</harvestWork>
      <maxMeshCount>4</maxMeshCount>
      <visualSizeRange>0.4~0.7</visualSizeRange>
      <topWindExposure>0.35</topWindExposure>
      <wildOrder>1</wildOrder>
      <fertilityMin>0.05</fertilityMin>
      <fertilitySensitivity>0</fertilitySensitivity>
    </plant>
  </ThingDef>

  <!-- ============== Vault-root tree — RUT_Wasteland ============== -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="TreeBase">
    <defName>RUT_VaultRoot</defName>
    <label>vault-root tree</label>
    <description>A squat, gnarled tree whose swollen trunk is seamed with dull metallic veins -- it has spent decades sequestering what it drinks out of the ground into itself. Prospectors call felling one "opening the vault," and know exactly what that name is warning them about.</description>
    <minifiedDef IsNull="True" />
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>190</MaxHitPoints>
      <Nutrition>1.6</Nutrition>
      <Mass>90</Mass>
    </statBases>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Plant/VaultRoot</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Random</graphicClass>
      <shadowData>
        <volume>(0.22, 0.28, 0.15)</volume>
        <offset>(0,0,-0.36)</offset>
      </shadowData>
    </graphicData>
    <fillPercent>0.32</fillPercent>
    <plant>
      <lifespanDaysPerGrowDays>45</lifespanDaysPerGrowDays>
      <fertilityMin>0.05</fertilityMin>
      <fertilitySensitivity>0</fertilitySensitivity>
      <growDays>18</growDays>
      <harvestWork>220</harvestWork>
      <harvestYield>22</harvestYield>
      <harvestedThingDef>WoodLog</harvestedThingDef>
      <harvestMinGrowth>0.2</harvestMinGrowth>
      <topWindExposure>0.06</topWindExposure>
      <visualSizeRange>1.2~2.6</visualSizeRange>
      <wildClusterRadius>-1</wildClusterRadius>
      <treeLoversCareIfChopped>true</treeLoversCareIfChopped>
    </plant>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
